From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 13:42:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Expose first_strong_direction for HTML dir=auto resolution

HTML's dir=auto directionality is a DOM-side scan (it excludes bdi/
script/style/textarea subtrees and dir-attributed descendants),
which a text-stream resolver cannot express. The embedder walks
text nodes itself and needs only the per-chunk classification.
Classifies via the same parley_data properties analyze_text uses:
strong L is Ltr, strong R or AL is Rtl, and anything else is None, so
the caller keeps walking.

The classifier lives in parley_engine, which owns the parley_data
properties; parley re-exports it as parley::first_strong_direction
(returning parley::BaseDirection) in the parley series.
---
 src/bidi.rs | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 src/lib.rs  |  1 +
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/bidi.rs b/src/bidi.rs
index 0e88be4..bf85bcd 100644
--- a/src/bidi.rs
+++ b/src/bidi.rs
@@ -7,6 +7,24 @@ use alloc::vec::Vec;
 use icu_properties::props::{BidiClass, BidiMirroringGlyph, BidiPairedBracketType};
 use parlance::{BaseDirection, BidiLevel};

+// First-strong scan for HTML's dir=auto directionality.
+// Callers walk DOM text nodes and stop at the first Some, applying
+// the spec's subtree exclusions themselves. This only classifies
+// one text chunk: strong L is Ltr, strong R or AL is Rtl.
+/// Returns the direction of the first strong character in `text`, or `None` if it has none.
+pub fn first_strong_direction(text: &str) -> Option<BaseDirection> {
+    for ch in text.chars() {
+        match parley_data::Properties::get(ch).bidi_class() {
+            BidiClass::LeftToRight => return Some(BaseDirection::Ltr),
+            BidiClass::RightToLeft | BidiClass::ArabicLetter => {
+                return Some(BaseDirection::Rtl);
+            }
+            _ => {}
+        }
+    }
+    None
+}
+
 /// Resolver for the Unicode bidirectional algorithm.
 #[derive(Clone, Default)]
 pub(crate) struct BidiResolver {
diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
index 647f360..396cf2e 100644
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -120,6 +120,7 @@ pub use parlance::{BaseDirection, NormalizedCoord};

 pub use analysis::{Analysis, AnalysisDataSources, CharInfo};
 pub use analyzer::{AnalysisOptions, Analyzer, LineBreakConfig};
+pub use bidi::first_strong_direction;
 pub use glyph::Glyph;
 pub use shape::atom::{Atom, Atoms, Grapheme, Graphemes, ShapedClusterGlyphs, ShapedSlice};
 pub use shape::shaped_text::{FontMetrics, ShapedRun, ShapedText};
